  "notes": "{浴|あ}びる means to pour or receive something over oneself. It has both a literal sense (water, shower) and a figurative sense (attention, criticism).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を for what is received\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{浴|あ}びている describes the ongoing state of being showered with or exposed to something.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- シャワーを{浴|あ}びる: to take a shower\n- {水|みず}を{浴|あ}びる: to pour water over oneself\n- {日光|にっこう}を{浴|あ}びる: to bask in sunlight\n- {注目|ちゅうもく}を{浴|あ}びる: to attract attention\n- {批判|ひはん}を{浴|あ}びる: to receive criticism\n- {拍手|はくしゅ}を{浴|あ}びる: to receive applause\n\nCONTRAST:\nFor bathing in a tub, use お{風呂|ふろ}に{入|はい}る, not {浴|あ}びる. {浴|あ}びる implies something coming down onto you, not immersion.",
